# The Debian packages a fresh Yantrik install has, and an updated one gets (#854).
#
# One list, read by both sides, so they cannot drift:
#   build-debian-iso.sh  installs every name here into the image, with no `|| true`: a desktop
#                        missing its runtime is a failed build.
#   yantrik-update       after an apply (and on `reconcile`), installs whichever of these this
#                        machine lacks. It reads the copy the release bundle ships at
#                        /opt/yantrik/share/packages.list, and only when that file is root's and
#                        its sha256 is the one in bin/yantrik-root-files.sha256.
# Before this, the ISO had its list and yantrik-update had a second one typed into it, and mpv
# was only in the first: a machine installed before #255 never got a player, and Music could not
# play (#854).
#
# Format: one Debian package name per line; `#` starts a comment. A line that is not exactly one
# name ([a-z0-9][a-z0-9+.-]+, not ending in `-`, which apt-get reads as "remove") makes the whole
# list refused, by the image build and the updater alike. Both pass the names to apt as separate
# arguments, never through a shell, and only names the mirror has exactly: apt-get would read
# any other name with `.` or `+` in it as a regex.
#
# What is NOT here: the kernel, the boot loader, live-boot, firmware, mbpfan, guest tools and the
# installer's own tools. The image installs those in its own steps, some only where they fit the
# hardware, and an installed machine must never be given live-boot or the other boot loader.

# ── The desktop's own runtime ──
# What a machine built from cloud-init/user-data.yaml gets, because the same shell runs on both.
seatd
libcap2-bin
chromium
pipewire-pulse
wireplumber
pulseaudio-utils
python3-websocket
fontconfig
# The capture bar (design/capture-2026-10-15.md): the screenshot, the region a person drags, the
# recording, and whether the GPU encodes H.264, asked before a recording starts. wf-recorder's
# libav libraries are mpv's too.
grim
slurp
wf-recorder
vainfo
qemu-guest-agent
libnotify-bin
# xdg-desktop-portal-gtk is the file picker behind every Save and Upload the browser offers (#33).
xdg-desktop-portal
xdg-desktop-portal-wlr
xdg-desktop-portal-gtk
lxpolkit
udisks2
brightnessctl
# The battery reading and the power profile (story 1.4). yantrik-update skips
# power-profiles-daemon on a machine with tlp: they conflict, and apt would remove tlp.
upower
power-profiles-daemon
bluez
alsa-utils
# Music and Files play sound and video in mpv (#255, #728).
mpv
# The Package Manager installs Flathub apps with it, per-user and without root (#399).
flatpak
nftables

# ── Programs the shell shells out to by name ──
#   swaybg     yantrik-companion-tools/src/wallpaper.rs, and the label Mind View shows while empty
#   xdg-utils  mime_dispatch.rs and lens.rs call xdg-open to hand a file to its app
#   espeak-ng  the voice fallback when Piper is not the chosen engine
swaybg
xdg-utils
espeak-ng

# ── The person's own tools ──
# nano is what yantrik-session exports as EDITOR. vim-tiny: scripts and muscle memory call `vi`
# (#678). release-check (tier ci) asserts these commands on the booted image.
nano
htop
vim-tiny

# ── A developer's baseline (#401) ──
# Rootless podman for the Container Manager, with what rootless needs beside it: uidmap
# (newuidmap/newgidmap), passt (pasta, podman 5's rootless network), fuse-overlayfs. Named rather
# than left to Recommends, because yantrik-update installs with --no-install-recommends.
git
bash-completion
podman
uidmap
passt
fuse-overlayfs

# ── Also installed by the image's earlier steps ──
# The image installs these before the list (debootstrap's --include, the network and Wayland
# steps), so naming them here changes nothing in a build that has them; they are here so an
# updated machine is given them too (#210: VM 520 had no `ip`, `ss` or `ping`). release-check
# asserts their commands on the booted image. python3 runs yos.
iproute2
iputils-ping
wl-clipboard
curl
python3
